From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 09:32:12 +0000
Subject: editing: Hoist UpdateStyleAndLayout out of SelectionHasFocus()

SelectionHasFocus() ran Document::UpdateStyleAndLayout() before reading
the selection, and IsHidden() calls it. Two of their callers run inside
a lifecycle update, where the tree must already be clean and a forced
update is not allowed: LayoutSelection::Commit() from the compositing
inputs phase, and FrameCaret::UpdateAppearance()/paint. Crash reports
show the compositing-inputs case reached from a drag-over hit test
(DragController::DragEnteredOrUpdated -> LocalFrame::DocumentAtPoint ->
LayoutView::HitTest -> UpdateAllLifecyclePhasesExceptPaint ->
LayoutView::CommitPendingSelection -> LayoutSelection::Commit ->
FrameSelection::IsHidden -> SelectionHasFocus ->
Document::UpdateStyleAndLayout), ending in the
StateAllowsTreeMutations() CHECK in
UpdateStyleAndLayoutTreeForThisDocument().

Hoist the update to the callers that run outside a lifecycle update (the
crbug.com/590369 TODO): MoveCommands, EditorKeyBindings,
DragController::DragIsMove and the clipboard commands now update first;
editor commands, SelectionController and EventHandler already did. The
lifecycle-time callers read the current tree, as their own DCHECKs
already require.

The test reproduces the crash state: a pending selection commit and
style dirtied after layout, then the hit-test lifecycle update. It is
release-only because LayoutSelection::Commit() DCHECKs the tree clean
first; how the tree gets dirty at that point in the field is not
identified, and that DCHECK keeps flagging it in debug builds.

Bug: 541952000
Test: blink_unittests --gtest_filter=LocalFrameViewTest.CompositingInputsCommitsPendingSelectionWithoutUpdatingDirtyStyle

Backport of https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8252692

